# Hexagonal Architecture (TanStack Start adaptation)

Follow a **feature-module hexagonal** layout. Each feature owns its layers. Wire dependencies only in the composition root.

## Dependency flow

```
Routes / React UI (src/routes/, module presentation/)
  → server functions (modules/<feature>/server/) — driving adapters
  → use case interfaces (GetPublicCatalog, SaveResource, …)
  → use case implementations (*UseCase)
  → domain port (CatalogPort) — only for I/O-bound use cases
  → adapters (D1CatalogAdapter, BetterAuthSessionAdapter)
  → Zod schemas + mappers
  → getDb() / Better Auth / external I/O
  → D1, Better Auth API
```

Pure use cases (e.g. filter parsing, in-memory search) do not call a port.

Routes and components must call a module's **public server API** or DI-provided use cases — never adapters, D1, or `getDb()` directly.

## Project layout

```
src/
  app/
    config/env.ts              # Zod-validated env at startup
    di/                        # composition root (*.module.ts)
    router.tsx                 # TanStack Router instance (if not colocated in routes/)
  modules/<feature>/             # vertical slice per feature (catalog, library, identity)
    domain/
      entities/                # domain models (camelCase)
      errors/                  # domain error types (CatalogNotFound, Unauthorized, …)
      ports/                   # outbound contracts (CatalogPort)
    application/
      <use-case>/              # interface + *UseCase per folder (get-public-catalog/, …)
      index.ts
    adapters/
      d1/                      # or better-auth/, etc.
      schemas/                 # Zod DTOs (snake_case / row shapes stay here)
      mappers/                 # validated DTO / row → domain entity
      errors/                  # map infra failures → domain/port errors
    server/                    # thin createServerFn handlers (driving adapters)
    presentation/              # feature-specific components (optional)
    index.ts                   # public exports for routes and other modules
  shared/
    domain/                    # Result.ts and cross-module domain primitives
    adapters/                  # shared infra (if needed)
    db.ts                      # getDb() accessor
    utils/
  routes/                      # TanStack Start file-based routes — loaders call modules
  integrations/                # cross-cutting UI glue (auth header, etc.)
```

**MVP modules:** `catalog`, `library`, `identity`.

Migrate incrementally from flatter paths (e.g. `ports/` at module root, plain functions instead of `*UseCase`) toward this layout.

## Nomenclature

| Concept | Name in this repo |
| ------- | ----------------- |
| Outbound domain contract | `CatalogPort` (`domain/ports/`) |
| D1 / auth implementation | `D1CatalogAdapter`, `BetterAuthSessionAdapter` (`adapters/d1/`, `adapters/better-auth/`) |
| Application contract | `GetPublicCatalog`, `SaveResource` (no `Port` suffix) |
| Application implementation | `GetPublicCatalogUseCase`, etc. |
| Legacy `infrastructure/` | Use `adapters/` |
| Legacy `*Repository` | Use `*Port` (domain) or `*Adapter` (implementations) |
| Persistence row / API DTO | Zod schema in `adapters/schemas/`, mapped in `adapters/mappers/` |

**Rule:** the `Port` suffix is reserved for **domain** outbound contracts only.

## Composition root (`src/app/di/`)

- Only `src/app/di/*.module.ts` may instantiate `getDb()`, adapters, use cases, and server-function dependencies.
- Example: `catalog.module.ts` wires `getDb()` → `D1CatalogAdapter` → `GetPublicCatalogUseCase` → exports wired deps for `modules/catalog/server/`.
- Routes, React components, and use cases must not construct adapters or call `getDb()` directly.
- Tests may construct adapters inline or via test doubles; production wiring goes through DI modules.
- Prefer factory functions over DI frameworks; one `*.module.ts` per feature is enough for MVP.

## Rules

### Domain (`modules/<feature>/domain/`)

- Must not import React, TanStack, D1, Better Auth, SQL, `fetch`, Zod, adapters, or routes.
- `entities/` holds business types and pure rules.
- `errors/` holds domain error types used in `Result<T, E>`.
- `ports/` holds outbound contracts (`CatalogPort`).
- Uses camelCase. D1 `snake_case` must not appear here.

### Application (`modules/<feature>/application/`)

- One folder per use case (`get-public-catalog/`, `save-resource/`).
- Each folder exports a use case **interface** (no `Port` suffix) and a `*UseCase` class that implements it.
- I/O-bound use cases depend on domain **port interfaces**, never on concrete adapters or `getDb()`.
- Pure logic use cases depend only on domain entities and other use case interfaces.
- Return `Result<T, DomainError>` for expected failures; do not throw on the happy path.
- No SQL, HTTP, or Zod in application code.

### Adapters (`modules/<feature>/adapters/`)

- Implement domain ports (`*Adapter` naming).
- Own all I/O: D1 prepared statements, Better Auth, external HTTP.
- `schemas/` — Zod schemas for rows, request payloads, and external DTOs.
- `mappers/` — convert validated schemas to domain entities (`mapResourceRowToEntity`).
- `errors/` — map D1/HTTP/validation failures to domain or port errors before returning `Result`.
- `snake_case` stays in schemas; domain entities are camelCase.

### Server (`modules/<feature>/server/`)

- Driving adapters: thin `createServerFn` handlers.
- Resolve wired use cases from `src/app/di/<feature>.module.ts`; instrument with Sentry spans (see `sentry.mdc`).
- Map `Result` errors to server-fn responses here, not in routes or components.

### Public API (`modules/<feature>/index.ts`)

- Export server functions, use case interfaces/types, and domain ports needed by other modules.
- Do **not** export adapters, mappers, schemas, or internal domain helpers unless tests require them.

### Presentation (`src/routes/`, `modules/<feature>/presentation/`)

- Route loaders call module server functions from `#/modules/<feature>`.
- Components render state and dispatch events. No business logic, SQL, auth enforcement, or adapter construction.
- Prefer loaders + server functions over client-side fetching for catalog and personal data.

## Cross-module dependencies

- **Allowed:** module A use case → module B **domain port** (via `#/modules/<feature>` public export).
- **Forbidden:** module A → module B adapters, schemas, mappers, or D1 code.
- **Forbidden:** circular module dependencies. Shared ports live in the owning module and are re-exported from its `index.ts`.

Example: `library` `SaveResourceUseCase` depends on `CatalogPort` from `catalog`, not on `D1CatalogAdapter`.

## Data boundaries (RutaSec)

- `catalog` module → editorial `resources` (read).
- `library` module → personal `user_resources` (write/read).
- Never mix editorial metadata with user progress in domain entities or use cases.

## Errors and Result

- Shared `Result<T, E>` lives in `src/shared/domain/result.ts`.
- Domain errors in `modules/<feature>/domain/errors/`.
- Adapter errors mapped in `modules/<feature>/adapters/errors/` before crossing into use cases.
- Use cases return `Result<T, DomainError>`; reserve throwing for unexpected infrastructure failures.
- Unwrap or map `Result` only in `server/` or `app/di/`, not in routes or components.

## SOLID (pragmatic)

- **Single responsibility:** one use case per folder; one module per bounded feature.
- **Open/closed:** extend via new use cases/adapters, not by editing another module's domain for UI needs.
- **Liskov:** port implementations honor the full contract (e.g. public catalog reads only published resources).
- **Interface segregation:** small ports per module, not one mega-repository.
- **Dependency inversion:** application depends on ports; adapters depend on domain shapes.

## Avoid

- Top-level `src/domain/`, `src/application/`, `src/ports/`, `src/adapters/` outside modules.
- Instantiating adapters or calling `getDb()` outside `src/app/di/` (except tests).
- SQL or Zod in routes, components, domain, or application layers.
- `*Port` on use case names.
- Leaking `snake_case` row fields into domain entities.

## Example (`catalog` module)

```
src/modules/catalog/
  domain/
    entities/resource.ts
    errors/catalog-errors.ts
    ports/catalog-port.ts
  application/
    get-public-catalog/
      get-public-catalog.ts          # interface GetPublicCatalog
      get-public-catalog.use-case.ts # class GetPublicCatalogUseCase
    index.ts
  adapters/
    d1/d1-catalog-adapter.ts
    schemas/resource-row.schema.ts
    mappers/map-resource-row.ts
    errors/map-d1-error.ts
  server/get-public-catalog.ts
  index.ts

src/app/di/catalog.module.ts
```

```ts
// domain/ports/catalog-port.ts
export interface CatalogPort {
  listPublished(filters: CatalogFilters): Promise<Result<CatalogResource[], CatalogError>>
}

// application/get-public-catalog/get-public-catalog.use-case.ts
export class GetPublicCatalogUseCase implements GetPublicCatalog {
  constructor(private readonly catalog: CatalogPort) {}
  async execute(input?: CatalogListInput): Promise<Result<PublicCatalog, CatalogError>> { /* … */ }
}

// app/di/catalog.module.ts
export function createCatalogModule(db: D1Database) {
  const catalog = createD1CatalogAdapter(db)
  return { getPublicCatalog: new GetPublicCatalogUseCase(catalog) }
}

// server/get-public-catalog.ts
export const getPublicCatalogFn = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })
  .handler(async ({ data }) =>
    Sentry.startSpan({ name: 'getPublicCatalog' }, () => {
      const { getPublicCatalog } = createCatalogModule(getDb())
      return unwrap(await getPublicCatalog.execute(data))
    }),
  )

// routes/catalog/index.tsx
import { getPublicCatalogFn } from '#/modules/catalog'
```
